From 6b83963d01869599e25d38e207d7aa72d959d543 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Muse <muse@local>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 04:44:35 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] FSR 3 frame generation (2x) for RTX 30-series, via a C++
 bridge to the FidelityFX API 3.1

FG-only milestone, title's own upscaling, DLSS untouched. Rust never
hand-mirrors AMD structs: it loads fsr3_bridge.dll over a minimal C ABI
and the bridge, compiled against the real FidelityFX SDK 1.1.4 headers,
loads amd_fidelityfx_dx12.dll, creates the FG context, wraps the swap
chain, and runs the per-frame prepare/configure. The scaffold's
ffx_fsr3.dll did not exist (FSR 3.0 is source-only; 3.1 is the single
prebuilt signed DLL).

- crates/victory-gpu/src/fsr3.rs: bridge loader, env (VICTORY_FSR3_FG /
  VICTORY_FSR3_DIR / VICTORY_FSR3_QUALITY), lazy FG context, note of
  depth/MV/camera from the title's upscale dispatch, present configure,
  in-place context remake on resize (the wrapped chain stays alive),
  mutual exclusion with DLSS FG, soft-fail everywhere.
- tools/fsr3-bridge: the bridge (create/wrap/prepare/configure/
  recreate/destroy) and its CMake build.
- fidelityfx.rs: interpose when Streamline or FSR 3 serves; FSR path
  notes the upscale and runs the title's own upscaler; the context
  size clamp stays DLSS-only.
- host.rs: device hand-over, submitted/resize hooks, swap-chain wrap
  in presenter(), FSR configure around Present, FG-aware FPS texts.
- run.rs / play.rs / play-foxhound.ps1 / menu.rs: init, -Fsr3FrameGen
  / --fsr3-framegen, victory get-fsr3, F1 live toggle (OFF/2X).
- Get-FSR3.cmd / scripts/get-fsr3.ps1: fetch SDK 1.1.4, build the
  bridge, copy both DLLs into fsr3-sdk/ (git-ignored).
- docs/FSR3_INTEGRATION.md: rewritten to describe what is built.

Not verifiable on Linux: no Rust toolchain here, and the bridge needs
Windows + MSVC + the SDK headers, then a 3080 Ti + the game for FG
context creation, depth/MV tagging, pacing, VRAM headroom and resize
behaviour.
